{"t": 815.99, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE_Diodes", "rationale": "The previous SSHI failed because the L-S inversion branch interfered with the rectifier, effectively shorting the piezo. I am switching to a Synchronized Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) approach. By using switches to connect the piezo to the output only at the voltage peaks via diodes, we can increase the energy extraction efficiency compared to a standard Full-Bridge Rectifier (FBR) while avoiding the continuous diode drop. This should lift vavg in S2 and S4. A Zener clamp is included to prevent vout_max violations in S3, and a storage capacitor will be tuned to balance startup time and ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE_Diodes", "rationale": "The previous SSHI failed because the L-S inversion branch interfered with the rectifier, effectively shorting the piezo. I am switching to a Synchronized Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) approach. By using switches to connect the piezo to the output only at the voltage peaks via diodes, we can increase the energy extraction efficiency compared to a standard Full-Bridge Rectifier (FBR) while avoiding the continuous diode drop. This should lift vavg in S2 and S4. A Zener clamp is included to prevent vout_max violations in S3, and a storage capacitor will be tuned to balance startup time and ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "neg"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
