{"t": 1384.48, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 4, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SyncRect_SECE", "rationale": "The FBR failed on S4 because the open-circuit voltage (1.9V) minus two diode drops (0.5V) is below the 1.8V target. To solve this, I am proposing a Synchronous Rectifier SECE. By using SYNC switches to handle the return path to ground, the circuit reduces the voltage drop to a single diode per half-cycle. S1 and S2 act as a synchronous pair during the positive peak, and S3 and S4 act as a pair during the negative peak. This maximizes the available voltage and should allow the output to reach 1.8V even under weak excitation (S4).", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SyncRect_SECE", "rationale": "The FBR failed on S4 because the open-circuit voltage (1.9V) minus two diode drops (0.5V) is below the 1.8V target. To solve this, I am proposing a Synchronous Rectifier SECE. By using SYNC switches to handle the return path to ground, the circuit reduces the voltage drop to a single diode per half-cycle. S1 and S2 act as a synchronous pair during the positive peak, and S3 and S4 act as a pair during the negative peak. This maximizes the available voltage and should allow the output to reach 1.8V even under weak excitation (S4).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "S3", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzn", "n1"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "S4", "type": "S", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "neg"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
