{"t": 1627.9, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 5, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Symmetric_SECE", "rationale": "The previous designs suffered from 'underpower' because the full-bridge rectifier clamped the piezo voltage, preventing it from reaching its open-circuit voltage and ruining the SSHI inversion. I am replacing the rectifier with a Synchronized Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. In SECE, the piezo is disconnected from the load during the charging phase and only connected during a very short pulse via an inductor. This prevents clamping and allows for efficient charge transfer even when the load is heavy. Two switches are used to handle both half-cycles of the piezo excitation.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Symmetric_SECE", "rationale": "The previous designs suffered from 'underpower' because the full-bridge rectifier clamped the piezo voltage, preventing it from reaching its open-circuit voltage and ruining the SSHI inversion. I am replacing the rectifier with a Synchronized Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. In SECE, the piezo is disconnected from the load during the charging phase and only connected during a very short pulse via an inductor. This prevents clamping and allows for efficient charge transfer even when the load is heavy. Two switches are used to handle both half-cycles of the piezo excitation.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzn", "n1"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n1", "n2"], "value": 0.002}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 2e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 2e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "neg"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
