{"t": 2130.51, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 7, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "ChargePump_Doubler", "rationale": "The previous SSHI and FBR designs failed because the open-circuit voltage (Voc) on weak excitation (S4) is too low (approx 1.9V) to maintain the 1.8V output after the diode drops of a standard bridge. To solve this, I am using a voltage-doubler charge pump. This structure will effectively double the piezo voltage, ensuring the output stays above 1.8V even under weak excitation, while a Zener diode (DZ33) clamps the output to prevent it from exceeding 3.6V. This eliminates the need for synchronous switches which were underperforming and provides a more robust voltage level for the load.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "ChargePump_Doubler", "rationale": "The previous SSHI and FBR designs failed because the open-circuit voltage (Voc) on weak excitation (S4) is too low (approx 1.9V) to maintain the 1.8V output after the diode drops of a standard bridge. To solve this, I am using a voltage-doubler charge pump. This structure will effectively double the piezo voltage, ensuring the output stays above 1.8V even under weak excitation, while a Zener diode (DZ33) clamps the output to prevent it from exceeding 3.6V. This eliminates the need for synchronous switches which were underperforming and provides a more robust voltage level for the load.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n1", "0"], "value": 1e-07}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C2", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n2", "0"], "value": 1e-07}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-05}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
